    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300-a1">

                <pb facs="0615" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg491"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    254.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Busch to Mr.
                            Everett</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-09-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 21,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor to state, in reply to the esteemed note of the 25th
                    ultimo, of the chargé d’affaires of the United States of America, Mr. H. Sidney
                    Everett, that he did not fail at the proper time to transmit to the royal
                    Prussian officers named therein the invitation in which the present
                    representatives of the von Steuben family are invited in the name of the
                    President and people of the United States to attend the centennial celebration
                    of the capitulation of the English army at Yorktown as guests of the
                    government.</p>
                <p>The undersigned is gratified to be able to inform the chargé d’affaires to-day
                    that the officers referred to gladly accept the invitation by which they have
                    been honored.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of this occasion, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>BUSCH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
